    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Darlington-Campus/Senior-Engineer-Supervisor--Large-Scale-Additive-Manufacturing_0156573-2": {
      "title": "Senior Engineer Supervisor: Large-Scale Additive Manufacturing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFull time, continuing opportunity Play a key role in supporting the operations of a world-class advanced manufacturing research facility Base Salary $152,045 - $160,430 + 17% superannuation About the opportunity As the Senior Engineer Supervisor: Large Scale Additive Manufacturing , you will lead the operations of the Sydney Manufacturing Hub's (SMH) G08 Large-format Additive Manufacturing Node, a critical research facility supporting cutting-edge research, and industry collaboration. Working closely with the SMH Management Team, researchers, students and industry partners, you will ensure the facility operates efficiently, safely and in alignment with the University's strategic research objectives. This is a unique opportunity to combine technical expertise, operational leadership and industry engagement in a highly visible role. You will oversee specialised equipment and facility operations, provide expert technical support to research programs, drive continuous improvement initiatives and foster partnerships that translate research capability into industry impact. Your key responsibilities will be to: oversee the day-to-day operations of the SMH G08 facility, ensuring services, infrastructure and resources effectively support research and industry related activities provide expert technical advice and support to researchers, students and industry partners using advanced manufacturing technologies and equipment lead industry engagement initiatives, identify opportunities for collaboration and deliver projects that create value for external partners manage facility expenditure, procurement activities and equipment maintenance to ensure efficient and sustainable operations ensure compliance with work health and safety requirements, risk management processes and relevant legislative obligations oversee facility documentation, reporting, data management and security requirements to support operational and regulatory compliance provide leadership, coaching and development support to technical staff while contributing to the strategic growth of the Sydney Manufacturing Hub About you postgraduate qualifications in engineering, manufacturing, materials, research infrastructure or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant training and experience demonstrated experience managing research facilities, specialised equipment or advanced technical environments working knowledge of additive manufacturing technologies and their research or industry applications proven experience leading teams and managing staff performance, capability development and operational outcomes strong understanding and practical application of work health and safety requirements within laboratory, manufacturing or research settings experience supporting complex research activities, technical programs or specialist engineering projects and engaging with diverse stakeholder groups demonstrated ability to manage expenditure, prioritise competing demands and solve complex operational or technical challenges Sponsorship / work rights for Australia You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to be eligible to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment. Pre-employment checks and declarations  Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University.  Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement   At the University of Sydney, our shared values are trust, accountability and excellence and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTQIA+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.  We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Platinum Employer. Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .  How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.   For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Kale Claffey Recruitment Operations by email to kale.claffey@sydney.edu.au © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Sunday 20 September 2026 11:59 PM"
    },
    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Camperdown-Campus/Research-Fellow-in-Multi-Omics-Data-Science_0152856-1": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Multi-Omics Data Science",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFull‑time, 3-year fixed term opportunity with potential to extend Join the Snow Vision Accelerator to drive a new research and drug‑development initiative at the University of Sydney’s School of Mathematics and Statistics, Camperdown Campus Develop statistical and computational capability for multi‑omics data analysis and drug discovery Base Salary Level A/B $ $117,936 - $157,381 p.a + 17% superannuation About the opportunity We seek to appoint a Postdoctoral Research Associate / Research Fellow in Multi-Omics Data Science to work in the Snow Vision Accelerator at the University of Sydney, with a strong focus towards therapeutic discovery. The Snow Vision Accelerator is an ambitious research and drug development initiative focused on transforming the treatment of glaucoma by uncovering the molecular mechanisms through which aging and associated metabolic dysfunction increase the vulnerability of the optic nerve to injury and neurodegeneration. The program integrates cutting-edge biology, data science, and translational drug discovery to identify, validate, and target age-related pathways underlying glaucomatous damage, and to develop drugs and new therapies that boost optic nerve resilience and prevent vision loss. We are seeking to appoint a Postdoctoral Research Associate / Research Fellow within the bioinformatics and pathway discovery platform to be at the forefront of establishing statistical and computational analytical capability for drug discovery-based research using multi-omics data analysis. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to a uniquely integrated research environment, where computational, experimental, clinical and translational expertise are closely aligned within the SVA program, enabling researchers to work side by side and drive discovery through to translation The successful applicant will also be part of the Sydney Precision Data Science Centre , the Charles Perkins Centre, and the School of Mathematics and Statistics at the University of Sydney.  In this role, you will be required to: contribute significantly towards the research effort of the team with increasing autonomy lead research projects to develop and apply advanced data analysis and computational techniques for multi-omics data analysis and drug discovery collaborate with interdisciplinary teams to exchange ideas and leverage complementary expertise across statistics, data science, biology, and clinical and translational research maintain clear and comprehensive documentation of methods, data analyses, and findings for future reference and knowledge sharing contribute to, and assist in the joint supervision and training of research students contribute to bioinformatics and research dissemination workshops where required undertake administrative duties to support the management of the bioinformatics platform within the Snow Vision Accelerator. About you The University values courage and creativity; openness and engagement; inclusion and diversity; and respect and integrity. As such, we see the importance of recruiting talent aligned to these values and are looking for a Postdoctoral Research Associate / Research Fellow with the following selection criteria: completion (or near completion) of a PhD in statistics, data science, computer science, bioinformatics, or a related discipline research strengths in at least two of the following areas: statistical bioinformatics, computational bioinformatics, applied statistics, computer science, data science and computational biology. strong computational skills       demonstrated ability to conduct research / scholarly activities with limited supervision  demonstrated ability to work co-operatively and positively in a multidisciplinary research-based team environment and to engage with people from diverse backgrounds excellent interpersonal and both written and oral communication skills in English Applicants who demonstrate the following desirable criteria will be highly regarded: experience in analysing large-scale omics datasets in R or python strong general IT skills, including familiarity with Linux/Unix environments and HPC systems experience in assisting with the supervision of students undertaking undergraduate or higher degree research projects good organisational and administrative skills, with attention to detail Pre-employment checks Your employment is conditional upon the completion of all role required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement   At the University of Sydney, our shared values are  trust, accountability and excellence  and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to  diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of  Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People ,  women ,  people living with a disability ,  people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as  LGBTIQ+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.  We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Gold employer.  Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .  How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, response to the selection criteria, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.  For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Simon Drew, Recruitment Operations by email to recruitment.sea@sydney.edu.au © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Tuesday 06 October 2026 11:59 PM"
    },
    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Sydney/Senior-Project-Officer_0156048-2": {
      "title": "Senior Project Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPart time (0.4FTE, with possibility to increase to 0.6FTE in 2027) fixed term three years Great opportunity to coordinate project delivery, stakeholder engagement, and communications to ensure successful outcomes at the Sydney Conservatorium of Music HEO 7 Base Salary $117,133 - $127,610 p.a. pro rata + 17% superannuation  About the opportunity One of Australia's oldest and most prestigious music institutions, the Sydney Conservatorium of Music has been part of the University of Sydney since 1990, providing world-class music education, performance opportunities, and research. For more than a century, it has been at the heart of Australia's musical and cultural life, playing a pivotal role in shaping the nation's musical landscape. This is a rare opportunity to join a globally significant research program that sits at the intersection of music, creativity, and social impact. As the Senior Project Officer, you will work closely with Professor Liza Lim AM and a network of leading artists and researchers, you will play a central role in delivering projects, events, and partnerships that engage with urgent climate and social issues. If you enjoy building relationships, bringing complex projects to life, and working in a dynamic creative and research environment, this role offers the chance to make a meaningful contribution while collaborating with inspiring people in Australia and internationally. Your key responsibilities will be to: coordinate a diverse portfolio of projects, helping to deliver a world-leading research program with impact across the arts, research, and broader community lead the planning and delivery of conferences, workshops, and events across Australia and internationally shape and maintain the program's digital presence, ensuring website content remains current, engaging, and accessible drive project outcomes by tracking progress, preparing reports, and identifying opportunities to improve performance and delivery foster productive partnerships with researchers, artists, industry collaborators, and other stakeholders to support program success manage project budgets and financial processes, ensuring the effective use of resources and smooth program delivery. About you Demonstrated experience in project and program coordination, with the ability to manage competing priorities and deliver outcomes in a complex environment Strong event planning and stakeholder engagement capabilities, with experience coordinating events, workshops, conferences, or related activities Sound financial administration skills, including budget monitoring, expenditure tracking, and reporting excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders Strong organisational skills, attention to detail, and confidence using a range of digital systems and platforms The ability to work both autonomously and collaboratively as part of a high-performing team Experience within a university, research, arts, music, or environmental context would be advantageous. Sponsorship / work rights for Australia You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment. Pre-employment checks and declarations  Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University.  Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement   At the University of Sydney, our shared values are trust, accountability and excellence and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTQIA+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.  We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Platinum Employer. Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .  How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.   For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Rae Hao, Recruitment Operations by email to rae.hao@sydney.edu.au. © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Sunday 20 September 2026 11:59 PM"
    },
    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Camperdown-Campus/Technician-Commitment-Marketing-and-Communications-Officer_0156628-1": {
      "title": "Technician Commitment Marketing and Communications Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFull time, fixed term for 2 years Unique opportunity to deliver the newly-established Technician Commitment in Australia HEO 8 Base Salary $131,108 - $147868 + 17% superannuation  About the opportunity Microscopy Australia is the national collaborative research infrastructure providing researchers with access to world class microscopy, imaging and characterisation capabilities. Through a network of leading facilities hosted by the University of Sydney and partner universities and research organisations across Australia, Microscopy Australia supports cutting edge research, innovation and industry engagement across fields ranging from health and medicine to materials science and environmental research. The Technician Commitment is an internationally recognised initiative driving systemic and cultural change for technical and scientific professionals across higher education, research and innovation. Supported by a major Australian Government investment, this team will support the establishment and delivery of the Technician Commitment in Australia in partnership with Microscopy Australia, the Academy for Collaborative Research Infrastructure (ACRI), and the UK Technician Commitment team. As the Marketing and Communications Officer , you will play a key role in building the profile, visibility and impact of the newly established Technician Commitment in Australia. Working within the national Technician Commitment Australia team and reporting to the Program Lead, you will develop and deliver an integrated marketing and communications strategy across digital, print, media and event channels. You will create compelling content, manage the Technician Commitment's digital presence, secure positive media coverage and lead initiatives that raise awareness and engagement among technical professionals, institutional leaders, government, funders and the broader community. The role will work closely with the UK Technician Commitment team to maintain consistency with the global initiative's identity, branding and messaging while developing campaigns and communications tailored to Australian audiences. This is a unique opportunity to contribute to a nationally significant initiative that will strengthen technical career pathways, celebrate the contribution of technical professionals and support the future capability of Australia's research and innovation workforce. Your key responsibilities will be to: develop and deliver integrated marketing, communications and stakeholder engagement strategies that build awareness and recognition of the Technician Commitment across Australia create, manage and optimise content across digital, social media, website and email channels, ensuring messaging is engaging, accessible and aligned with brand standards identify, develop and promote compelling stories, campaigns and communications materials that showcase the impact of technical professionals and the Technician Commitment program drive media and public relations activities, including media releases, proactive story pitching, media engagement and support for spokespersons and key stakeholders work collaboratively with signatories, supporters, delivery partners and the UK Technician Commitment team to coordinate campaigns, events and communications activities monitor communications performance, media coverage and audience engagement, using insights and analytics to strengthen future communications and manage reputational issues where required. About you demonstrated experience in marketing, communications, media, public relations or a related field, including the development and delivery of multi-channel communications plans excellent writing, editing and storytelling skills, with experience producing high-quality digital, media and promotional content for diverse audiences proven experience managing websites, social media platforms, marketing campaigns and media relations activities, including securing positive media coverage ability to translate complex programs, research, evidence or policy issues into clear, engaging and audience-focused communications strong stakeholder engagement, organisational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and work effectively in a collaborative environment experience in higher education, research, research infrastructure or a similar sector would be advantageous, together with a commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and a relevant qualification or equivalent professional experience. Sponsorship / work rights for Australia You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment. Pre-employment checks Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University. Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement   At the University of Sydney, our shared values are trust, accountability and excellence and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTIQ+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.  We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Platinum Employer. Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .  How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.   For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Lena Jiang, Recruitment Operations by email to lena.jiang@sydney.edu.au . © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Wednesday 30 September 2026 11:59 PM"
    },
    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Camperdown-Campus/Technician-Commitment-Partnership-and-External-Engagement-Manager_0156451-1": {
      "title": "Technician Commitment Partnership and External Engagement Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFull time, fixed term for 2 years Unique opportunity to deliver the newly-established Technician Commitment in Australia HEO 9 Base Salary $152,045 - $160,430 + 17% superannuation  About the opportunity Microscopy Australia is the national collaborative research infrastructure providing researchers with access to world class microscopy, imaging and characterisation capabilities. Through a network of leading facilities hosted by the University of Sydney and partner universities and research organisations across Australia, Microscopy Australia supports cutting edge research, innovation and industry engagement across fields ranging from health and medicine to materials science and environmental research. The Technician Commitment is an internationally recognised initiative driving systemic and cultural change for technical and scientific professionals across higher education, research and innovation. Supported by a major Australian Government investment, this team will support the establishment and delivery of the Technician Commitment in Australia in partnership with Microscopy Australia, the Academy for Collaborative Research Infrastructure (ACRI), and the UK Technician Commitment team. The Partnerships and External Engagement Manager will play a central role in building the reach, profile and influence of the Technician Commitment in Australia. Working across the higher education, research and innovation sectors, you will develop and deliver engagement strategies that attract new signatories and supporters, strengthen strategic partnerships, and enhance the visibility and impact of the initiative nationally. Reporting to the Program Lead and working closely with the Steering Board and the UK Institute for Technical Skills & Strategy, you will engage with senior leaders, government representatives, policymakers, funders and sector bodies to advance the Technician Commitment and support positive outcomes for Australia's technical workforce. Your key responsibilities will be to: lead the development and delivery of the Technician Commitment Australia partnerships and external engagement strategy, supporting the growth and influence of the initiative nationally build and maintain strategic relationships with senior leaders across universities, research organisations, government, funders, industry, professional bodies and other key stakeholders secure and support new and existing signatories, supporters and strategic partners, developing compelling engagement approaches that strengthen participation and impact identify and coordinate opportunities to influence policy, funding and sector priorities relating to technical skills, workforce capability and technical careers provide strategic advice, stakeholder intelligence and high-quality engagement materials to support programme development, decision-making and external representation represent the Technician Commitment at national forums, conferences and stakeholder meetings, working closely with Australian and UK partners to maximise reach and impact About you You will be an experienced and credible partnerships and engagement professional with the ability to build trusted relationships and influence senior stakeholders across Australia's higher education, research and policy communities. significant experience in partnerships, stakeholder engagement, business development, policy or external relations within higher education, research, government or a comparable sector strong understanding of the Australian higher education and research landscape, including policy and funding issues relating to workforce development, technical skills and research capability demonstrated success building strategic partnerships and influencing senior stakeholders across organisational, sector and government environments experience attracting organisations to participate in initiatives, networks, programmes or collaborative partnerships and translating strategic objectives into effective engagement approaches exceptional communication, negotiation and stakeholder management skills, with the credibility to represent the programme at senior national forums and sector events strong strategic judgement, organisational capability and commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion, with knowledge of technical professionals and technical services being highly desirable Sponsorship / work rights for Australia You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment. Pre-employment checks Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University. Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement   At the University of Sydney, our shared values are trust, accountability and excellence and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTIQ+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.  We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Platinum Employer. Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .  How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.   For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Lena Jiang, Recruitment Operations by email to lena.jiang@sydney.edu.au . © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Wednesday 30 September 2026 11:59 PM"
