    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Camperdown-Campus/CAPE-Operations-Lead_0156386-1": {
      "title": "CAPE Operations Lead",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFull time, Fixed Term until 2032 , Located at Camperdown Campus Play a key leadership role in establishing Australia's newest ARC Centre of Excellence Offering a competitive remuneration package including 17% superannuation along with a comprehensive range of employee benefits About the opportunity The ARC Centre of Excellence for Advanced Peptide and Protein Engineering (CAPE) is a nationally significant research initiative that will transform the engineering and translation of peptides and proteins, molecules that are fundamental to all life on Earth, for human and planetary benefit. Working in close partnership with the Centre Director Professor Richard Payne , and Deputy Director Professor Kate Jolliffe , the CAPE Operations Lead will play a critical role in establishing and driving the operational success of the ARC Centre of Excellence for Advanced Peptide and Protein Engineering (CAPE). As a key member of the Centre's leadership team, you will lead the development and implementation of governance, operational and strategic initiatives that support CAPE's ambitious research and translation agenda. Bringing together world-leading researchers, industry partners and emerging technologies, CAPE will harness Australia's unique scientific strengths to discover and engineer novel molecules, develop innovative \"new-to-nature\" peptide and protein structures, and pioneer sustainable production technologies. The Operations Lead will work across a national network of stakeholders to support impactful outcomes in agriculture, conservation and biotechnology, while enabling the Centre's outreach, education and engagement activities that will inspire the next generation of scientific innovators. Your key responsibilities will be to: lead the operational planning and delivery of CAPE's strategic objectives manage Centre governance, reporting and compliance requirements coordinate activities across partner institutions and stakeholder groups oversee financial, administrative and operational processes support the delivery of outreach, engagement and impact initiatives provide high-level advice and support to the Centre Director and leadership team About you tertiary qualifications in a relevant discipline, or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience demonstrated experience managing a large research centre demonstrated understanding of the Australian research funding landscape, including ARC funding and reporting requirements experience supporting governance, financial management, compliance and stakeholder engagement in a complex research environment previous experience working within an ARC Centre of Excellence or a similar environment (desirable) To keep our community safe, please be aware of our COVID safety precautions which form our conditions of entry for all staff, students and visitors coming to campus. Sponsorship / work rights for Australia You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to be eligible to apply. Pre-employment checks and declarations  Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University.  Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement   At the University of Sydney, our shared values are trust, accountability and excellence and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTQIA+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.  We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Platinum Employer. Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .  How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.   For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Rebecca Astar or Cherie Goodwin, Recruitment Operations by email to recruitment.sea@sydney.edu.au © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Friday 18 September 2026 11:59 PM"
    },
    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Camperdown-Campus/Associate-Lecturer-in-Pharmacy----Education-Focused-_0155837": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer in Pharmacy - (Education Focused)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\n2 full-time, 12-month fixed-term positions available at Camperdown Campus Fantastic opportunity to make a significant contribution to the education endeavours of the Sydney Pharmacy School Base Salary from $113,400 + 17% superannuation   About the opportunity   The Sydney Pharmacy School is internationally recognised for excellence in pharmacy education and research, driving innovation across medication management, pharmaceutical sciences, patient care and health policy. Our academics are committed to delivering outstanding education that prepares graduates to address the evolving healthcare needs of the community.   We are seeking to appoint two Associate Lecturers in Pharmacy (Education Focused) to join our collegial and high-performing academic community during an exciting period of growth and transformation. In this role, you will contribute to the delivery of outstanding education through teaching and supporting students across pharmacy and pharmacological sciences disciplines, while developing your expertise in higher education teaching, curriculum design and educational innovation.   As part of the Sydney Pharmacy School, you will collaborate with leading academics across the Faculty of Medicine and Health, the broader health sector, and the University’s multidisciplinary initiatives. This position offers an education-focused academic workload with a primary emphasis on teaching, learning and student support, alongside contributions to service, governance and engagement activities within the School and University.   This is an exciting opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to student learning, develop your educational portfolio under the guidance of experienced academics, and contribute to innovative teaching practices within a supportive and collaborative environment.   Key Responsibilities: Contribute to the delivery of outstanding education through high-quality teaching, learning, assessment and student support across pharmacy, pharmacology and related disciplines Contribute to curriculum design, review and educational innovation, supporting contemporary, engaging and evidence-based learning experiences that enhance student success Coordinate units of study and contribute to the development, implementation and evaluation of assessment practices that support student learning outcomes Work collaboratively with senior colleagues to develop expertise in higher education teaching, curriculum design and educational leadership Contribute to student engagement, outreach and recruitment activities, including school engagement, orientation and community-facing initiatives Undertake service and administrative responsibilities that support the effective operation of the School, Faculty and University Contribute to the strategic priorities of the School, Faculty and University through teaching, service and engagement activities Contribute positively to a collaborative and inclusive academic culture that values diversity, innovation, excellence and mutual respect Undertake other duties commensurate with the level and responsibilities of the position.   About You: A PhD in Pharmacy, Pharmacology, Pharmaceutical Sciences, or a closely related discipline, or evidence of near completion Demonstrated expertise in pharmacy, pharmacology or pharmaceutical sciences, with the ability to contribute to teaching across relevant areas of the Sydney Pharmacy School Experience in teaching and learning within higher education and/or professional settings, including curriculum development, assessment design, laboratory, tutorial or classroom teaching A developing knowledge of contemporary pedagogical practice and evidence-based approaches to student learning and engagement Demonstrated ability to contribute to the design, implementation and evaluation of innovative teaching and learning initiatives. Experience working collaboratively as part of multidisciplinary teaching teams An understanding of current and emerging issues within the discipline and the higher education sector, with the capacity to contribute to educational priorities A commitment to fostering inclusive, equitable and respectful learning and working environments that support students and colleagues from diverse backgrounds Excellent interpersonal, communication and organisational skills, with the ability to contribute positively to a collaborative academic community. Work Rights You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment. Pre-employment checks Your employment is conditional upon the completion of all role-required pre-employment or background checks in terms satisfactory to the University. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement At the University of Sydney, our shared values include diversity and inclusion and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this commitment through our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability, people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTIQ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds. How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page. For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard. Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Rachel Yazigi , Recruitment Operations by email to rachel.yazigi@sydney.edu.au . © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Thursday 24 September 2026 11:59 PM"
    },
    "https://usyd.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/USYD_EXTERNAL_CAREER_SITE/job/Darlington-Campus/Research-Enterprise-Support-Officer_0155700-2": {
      "title": "Research Enterprise Support Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFull time fixed term until 31/12/26 Opportunity to support the Deputy Dean (Research) and Research Services team on programs of research and strategic research initiatives at the Business School HEO 5 Base Salary $93,345- $104,515 p.a. + 17% superannuation  About the opportunity The Research Enterprise Support Officer provides high-level administrative and operational support to strategic research programs, initiatives, and stakeholders, ensuring the seamless coordination of research activities, governance, communications, and logistics across the Business School's research enterprise. Your key responsibilities will be to: coordinate and support research projects, initiatives, and programs through effective administration, documentation, and stakeholder engagement organise research events, workshops, training sessions, and meetings, including logistics, communications, agendas, minutes, and follow-up actions provide operational support for Research Hubs, including member onboarding, event coordination, record management, and responding to enquiries prepare and distribute research communications, reports, presentations, and updates to support the School's research community and strategic objectives assist with research administration activities, including reporting, budget tracking, funding scheme processes, compliance documentation, and research awards programs. About you Relevant tertiary qualification and/or demonstrated experience in research administration, higher education, or a related field. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build effective stakeholder relationships while exercising tact, discretion, and professionalism. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities, work independently, and deliver outcomes in a fast-paced environment. Proven analytical and problem-solving skills, with experience interpreting data, preparing reports, and supporting evidence-based decision-making. Experience working in a research-focused environment, with an understanding of research processes, literature reviews, and academic engagement activities Sponsorship / work rights for Australia You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this employment to be eligible to apply. Pre-employment checks and declarations  Your employment is conditional upon the successful completion of all pre-employment or background checks required for the role in terms satisfactory to the University.  Also, to meet the University’s obligations under the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Eliminate Gender-Based Violence you will be asked to declare if you have been investigated for, or found to engaged in, sexual harm or gender-based violence in the course of previous employment or in a legal process. Similarly, your ongoing employment is conditional upon the satisfactory maintenance of all relevant clearances and background check requirements. If you do not meet these conditions, the University may take any necessary step, including the termination of your employment. EEO statement   At the University of Sydney, our shared values are trust, accountability and excellence and we strive to be a place where everyone can thrive. We are committed to creating a University community that thrives through diversity and reflects the wider community that we serve. We deliver on this through our commitment to diversity and inclusion , evidenced by our people and culture programs, as well as key strategies to increase participation and support the careers of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People , women , people living with a disability , people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds , and those who identify as LGBTQIA+ . We welcome applications from candidates from all backgrounds.  We are proud to be recognised as an Australian Workplace Equality Index (AWEI) Platinum Employer. Find out more about our work on diversity and inclusion .  How to apply Applications (including a cover letter, CV, and any additional supporting documentation) can be submitted via the Apply button at the top of the page.   For employees of the University or contingent workers, please login into your Workday account and navigate to the Career icon on your Dashboard.  Click on USYD Find Jobs and apply. For a confidential discussion about the role, or if you require reasonable adjustment or any documents in alternate formats, please contact Rae Hao, Recruitment Operations by email to rae.hao@sydney.edu.au. © The University of Sydney The University reserves the right not to proceed with any appointment. Click to view the Position Description for this role. Applications Close Thursday 17 September 2026 11:59 PM"
